  HDL Wrapper). It is tagged with the SPDX identifier
  LicenseRef-AMD-Xilinx-Output-Products, a document-local reference (not an entry
  of the SPDX License List) to the AMD End User Licence Agreement and the Xilinx
  Export Control Statement under which Vivado grants the right to use and
  distribute its Output Products. It is not I2A2-UPM work and is not covered by
  the Apache-2.0 grant of this repository.

  Build-time AMD/Xilinx dependencies, not redistributed by this repository: the
  IP cores instantiated by name in src/bsp-tmpe627/tcl (xilinx.com:ip:xdma 4.2,
  axis_data_fifo 2.0, c_counter_binary 12.0, xlconcat 2.1, xlconstant 1.1,
  fifo_generator 13.2) and the Xilinx libraries the sources instantiate: xpm
  (xpm_cdc_handshake, in src/bsp-tmpe627/src/axiRegisters.vhd) and UNISIM
  primitives (in clock_buffer.vhd and tmpe_daq_wrapper.vhd only). Those libraries
  and cores are supplied by Vivado to anyone who runs the build, under their own
  licences. No .xci, .bd, .xpe, .lic, bitstream or XSA output product is
  tracked; prj/ and out/, which hold them, are git-ignored.


